WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
Imagine you run a poor country.

2
00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:07.170
Almost every car, fridge and
machine your people buy is imported.

3
00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:10.070
One plan: put high tariffs on imports,

4
00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.510
and build your own factories behind them.

5
00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:16.880
From the 1950s, much of Latin
America tried a plan like this.

6
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.400
So did India, before its 1991 reforms.

7
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.670
Others steered industry differently.

8
00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:25.370
So can a government make
a poor country richer

9
00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.280
by stepping in where
markets do too little?

10
00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.520
In this mission, you'll weigh
up protecting infant industries

11
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.520
against selling to the world.

12
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.950
Then you'll look at what
governments can do for health,

13
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.030
schooling and infrastructure.

14
00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:41.280
Your mission: find out when
the state should steer,

15
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.840
and when it should step back.
